{
  title: "Storyboard Demo",
  scroll_range: 600,
  snap_positions: [0, 300, 600],

  elements: [
    {
      // Background — always fully visible.
      html: "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;background:linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 50%, #0f3460 100%)'></div>",
      position: [0, 0],
      width: 100,
      height: 100,
    },

    // Scene 1: visible at scroll=0, crossfades out into scene 2 around scroll=260.
    {
      markdown: "## Scene One\n\nManual crossfade keyframes drive the per-element opacity ramps.",
      color: "#e0e0e0",
      position: [15, 25],
      width: 70,
      height: "auto",
      opacity: { keyframes: [[40, 1.0], [260, 0.0]] },
    },

    // Scene 2: fades in 40-260, holds 260-340, fades out 340-560.
    {
      markdown: "## Scene Two\n\nEach scene can contain multiple elements —\ntext, images, or raw HTML.",
      color: "#e0e0e0",
      position: [15, 25],
      width: 70,
      height: "auto",
      opacity: { keyframes: [[40, 0.0], [260, 1.0], [340, 1.0], [560, 0.0]] },
    },
    {
      html: "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;border:2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.3);border-radius:8px;box-sizing:border-box'></div>",
      position: [10, 60],
      width: 80,
      height: 25,
      opacity: { keyframes: [[40, 0.0], [260, 1.0], [340, 1.0], [560, 0.0]] },
    },

    // Scene 3: fades in 340-560.
    {
      markdown: "## Scene Three\n\nSnap positions settle the view\nonto each scene after scrolling stops.",
      color: "#e0e0e0",
      position: [15, 25],
      width: 70,
      height: "auto",
      opacity: { keyframes: [[340, 0.0], [560, 1.0]] },
    },
  ],
}
